## Why this case needed a tool written for it

  PIM-SSM is **defined** by the (S,G) join, and IGMPv2 cannot carry a source list, so the
  subject of this case could not be expressed with the tools the bench had.  `tools/igmp.py`
  was **extended with an IGMPv3 mode** (generic, in `tools/` with its README entry, not a
  case-local script): `-3`, `--source A[,B]`, `--record {is-include|is-exclude|to-include|
  to-exclude|allow|block}`, defaulting to `to-include` on join — what a real host sends when it
  joins an SSM channel — and to `to-include` with an EMPTY source list on leave, which is how
  IGMPv3 leaves an include-mode group.  Reports go to 224.0.0.22, v2 reports to the group and
  v2 leaves to 224.0.0.2; the tool picks the right destination and link-layer address for each.
  The v2 path is unchanged and was re-verified in T43863/T43864.

