VERDICT: PASS -- all three authored steps pass, including step 1's "IGMP Host joined the correct multicast source", which was measurable only because tools/igmp.py gained an IGMPv3 source-list mode for this case. The defining SSM property is proven on the wire: the joined channel forwards 9-10/10 while the SAME group from a DIFFERENT source is 0/10 in the same leg, at layer 3, both sharing one link-layer address. An IGMPv2 (*,G) join on the SSM range is rejected; the table state is pure SSM (zero (*,G), one (S,G), SPT bit set, no RP); prune on leave clears both tables; interface down/up behaves correctly with the two readings distinguished (O-28); and source filtering still holds after a cold boot. Produced F-14, O-27, O-28.
